---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_ORG } from '../config';
---

<Base title={SITE.name} bareTitle description={SITE.description}>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Tools for digital humanities</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Archives are not short of material. They are short of ways in.
        BabelStacks builds software for working with texts, collections, and
        the structures that make them navigable.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work on retrieval, indexing, and the unglamorous infrastructure
        that sits between a scanned page and a citable source.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where things stand</h2>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>We are early.</strong> Tools are in development and nothing
          is released yet. If your work overlaps with ours — or you have an
          archive that needs wrangling — we would like to hear from you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
          <a href={GITHUB_ORG} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The name</h2>
      <p>
        Borges imagined a library containing every book that could possibly be
        written. It holds all knowledge and is useless, because nothing in it
        can be found. The catalogue is in there too, along with every false
        catalogue.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the problem we care about. Digitisation has given us the
        library; it has not given us the catalogue.
        <a href="/about/">More about how we approach it →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5.5rem) 0;
  }
</style>
